      "Language": "slo",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In nuclear cardiology the exercise test is used above all to assess the diagnosis when ischaemic heart disease is suspected and to assess the extent and site of ischaemic heart disease. The objective of the submitted paper is to present new possibilities in this area where more perfect technical equipment and new methodological approaches contribute new quality to clinical decision taking. Greatest attention is devoted to tomographic analyses of perfusion of the heart muscle during the exercise test."},
